; Regression test for issue #3327: a lot price with no commodity totals a
; lot in no commodity.
;
; amount_t::price() multiplied a lot price by its lot, which gave the total
; the lot's commodity when the price had none.  So --basis reported
; C$100.00 held at a lot price of 1.50 as costing C$150.00 rather than
; 150.00.  And a report summed with -M, which measures its lots from their
; lot price, booked the difference as an unrealized loss.

2009/06/03 Opening
    Assets:Wallet                  C$100.00 {1.50}
    Equity:Opening

2009/06/04 Westjet
    Expenses:Transportation:Air    C$429.80 @ 1.572865
    Liabilities:Mastercard

test reg -B
09-Jun-03 Opening               Assets:Wallet                   150          150
                                Equity:Opening                 -150            0
09-Jun-04 Westjet               Expe:Transportatio:Air   676.017377   676.017377
                                Liabilities:Mastercard  -676.017377            0
end test

test bal -V --unrealized -M
            157.2865  Assets:Wallet
           -157.2865  Equity:Opening
          676.017377  Expenses:Transportation:Air
         -676.017377  Liabilities:Mastercard
--------------------
                   0
end test
